# =============================================================================
# numerus — Sized primitive family violation (expect type error).
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Type family restriction — the retired wrapped form `numerus<W>` rejects float width markers; write the bare float marker (`f32`)
#   • Compile-time error — type family violations are caught and reported at compile time
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • writing the retired `numerus<f32>` for a floating-point type — width families are type-specific; the bare `f32` is the float spelling
#
# See also: numerus, fractus
# =============================================================================




# sized primitive family violation (expect type error)
#
# WHY: the retired wrapped form `numerus<W>` rejects float width markers; the bare `f32` is the float spelling.
#
# DELIBERATE: this exemplum keeps the retired spelling (`int<f32>`) on purpose, to
# pin the SEM002 family diagnostic until the parser rejects the wrapped forms (N7d).

main {
    const int<f32> invalid ← 1.0 ∷ f32
    print invalid
}